Let the int8-QK prefill attention fire for any 6:1 GQA layout (fork).

prefill-attn-int8.patch gates its kernel on the single-card geometry, 24 q-heads
/ 4 kv-heads. Under --tensor-parallel-size 2 every rank holds 12 / 2 (and 6 / 1
at TP=4), the same G=6 the kernel was measured on, and it is written over HKV
and G, so the gate only shut it out. Measured on 2x RTX 3090 at TP=2
(FLASH_ATTN, bf16 KV, INT8_ACT=int8, host-staged all-reduce): 8k 3,160 -> 3,199
tok/s, 32k 2,775 -> 2,802, 128k 1,794 -> 1,838.

